Value VLAN_ID (\d+)
Value NAME (\S+)
Value STATUS (\S+)

Start
  ^VLAN\s+Name\s+Status\s+Ports\s*$$
  ^-+\s+-+\s+-+\s+-+\s*$$
  ^${VLAN_ID}\*?\s+${NAME}\s+${STATUS}(?:\s+\S.*)?\s*$$ -> Record
  # Ports that do not fit on the line continue on the next, indented: membership is read elsewhere.
  ^\s+\S
  # A footnote such as "* indicates a Dynamic VLAN" follows the table when one is listed.
  ^\*\s
  ^\s*$$
  ^. -> Error

# EOS refuses a VLAN name with a space, so NAME is one word. Internal VLANs of routed ports are not
# listed by this command (feature 008, research R1).
